WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.487
Module fourteen:

2
00:00:01.487 --> 00:00:04.329
taxes and rules, an overview by country.

3
00:00:04.329 --> 00:00:06.888
This is an overview, not tax advice:

4
00:00:06.888 --> 00:00:10.156
the rules change every year, so before filing,

5
00:00:10.156 --> 00:00:13.070
check with your tax office or an adviser.

6
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.512
In most countries a coin is property.

7
00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:20.340
Tax arises not when you buy, but when the coin leaves you:

8
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.858
sold, swapped or spent.

9
00:00:21.858 --> 00:00:27.006
Almost everywhere gains are taxed, swapping one coin for another is taxed too.

10
00:00:28.006 --> 00:00:31.643
The second question is how the tax office sees the profit.

11
00:00:31.643 --> 00:00:34.152
If you hold coins and sell now and then,

12
00:00:34.152 --> 00:00:38.228
it is usually a capital gain with a separate, often reduced rate.

13
00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:42.994
If trading looks like a job, with frequent trades, a bot and an aim to earn,

14
00:00:42.994 --> 00:00:46.318
the profit may be treated as income at the full rate.

15
00:00:47.318 --> 00:00:52.425
The third question is which purchase price to deduct if you bought several times.

16
00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:54.002
The method is set by law:

17
00:00:54.002 --> 00:00:57.343
in order of purchase, by average price, or otherwise.

18
00:00:57.343 --> 00:01:00.938
The method determines how much profit lands in this year.

19
00:01:00.938 --> 00:01:05.730
So for every trade keep the date, quantity, price in local currency and fee,

20
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.630
and download your exchange history every year.

21
00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.608
Tax is paid in the country of tax residency, not in the exchange's country.

22
00:01:14.608 --> 00:01:19.254
A resident pays tax on trades on any exchange, including foreign ones.
